the target language is: prolog.

% The British Nationality Act 1981, in Logical English.
%
% Recovered from a 1980s micro-PROLOG program on a floppy disk ("DISK IMAGE.txt"),
% (Paper authors, https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/5689.5920: 
%    M. J. Sergot, F. Sadri, R. A. Kowalski, F. Kriwaczek, P. Hammond, H. T. Cory )
% ...and translated from its SWI-Prolog conversion, bna.pl. bnaRecovery.md, section 10,
% says which clauses were chosen, what was reconstructed, and what was assumed.
%
% Every rule is labelled with the section of the Act it comes from ("with provenance").
% The comment above each rule gives the byte offset, in the disk image, of the clause
% it is translated from. "reconstructed" marks a rule pieced together from damaged
% copies, or written by analogy where the original is lost.
%
% Dates are Logical English dates (1985-01-01). The original's own date arithmetic
% (sumdate, days-in-month and so on) is replaced by the date templates of
% Logical English.
%
% A condition the original "asked about" or merely advised on ("formal consent is
% required", "on making an application ...") is an assumable template here: when the
% facts of a case do not settle it, the answer lists it as an unknown.

the templates are:
% --- the questions of the original system
*a person* is a british citizen on *a date*.
*a person* is a british citizen by descent on *a date*.
*a person* is a british citizen by annulment of renunciation on *a date*.
*a person* is entitled to register as a british citizen on *a date*.
*a person* is entitled to naturalise as a british citizen on *a date*.
*a person* is entitled to renounce british citizenship on *a date*.
the question is asked on *a date*.

% --- how a person is a british citizen, and under which section
*a person* is a british citizen by *a way* under section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* is entitled to register as a british citizen as *a category* under section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* is entitled to naturalise as a british citizen under section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* regains british citizenship by annulment of renunciation under section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* ceases to be a british citizen through renunciation under section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* is entitled to renounce british citizenship under section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* becomes a british citizen from *a date* by adoption under section *a section*.
*a person* satisfies section *a section* on *a date*.
*a person* satisfies section *a section* on *a date* for an application made on *a second date*.
*a person* satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4).
*a person* satisfies the residence requirement of section 3(3)(c) from *a date* to *a second date*.
*a person* satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4) from *a date* to *a second date*.

% --- dates
*a date* is the commencement date.
*a date* is on or after commencement.
*a date* is prior to commencement.
*a date* is the day before *a second date*.
*a date* is the eve of commencement.
*a date* is in the period from *a start* to *an end*.
*a second date* is *a number* years after *a first date*.
*a date* is within *a number* years after *a second date*.
*a date* is within *a number* years of commencement.
*a date* is the earlier of *a second date* and the death of *a person*.
*a date* is the earlier date of *a second date* and *a third date*.
*a second date* is six months on from *a first date*.

% --- persons and families
*a person* is born on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is born in *a place*; undefined.
the birthplace of *a person* is in the UK.
the birthplace of *a person* is outside the UK.
*a person* is born after commencement.
*a person* is born before commencement.
*a person* is born outside the UK after commencement.
*a person* is born stateless; undefined.
*a person* is *a number* years old on *a date*.
*a person* is a minor from *a date* to *a second date*.
*a person* is a minor on *a date*.
*a person* is a minor at commencement.
*a person* attains full age on *a date*.
*a person* is of full age on *a date*.
*a person* is of full age for section 12(5) on *a date*.
*a person* is of full capacity.
*a person* is of unsound mind; undefined.
*a person* is female; undefined.
*a person* is dead; undefined.
*a person* died on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* died before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* had died by commencement.
*a person* is the mother of *a second person*; undefined.
*a person* is the father of *a second person*; undefined.
*a person* is a parent of *a second person*.
*a person* is the paternal grandfather of *a second person*.
both parents of *a person* are alive on *a date*; undefined.
the mother of *a person* was dead on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was married on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* had married by *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is married on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was married to *a second person* on or before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is the wife of *a second person* on *a date*.
*a person* is the husband of *a second person* on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is adopted as a minor by an order of a UK court on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is an adopter of *a second person*; undefined.

% --- presence in the UK
*a person* was in the UK on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was absent from the UK for *a number* days from *a date* to *a second date*; undefined.
*a person* was in the UK in breach of the immigration laws from *a date* to *a second date*; undefined.
*a person* is ordinarily resident in the UK on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is subject to no restriction on the period for which he may remain in the UK on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is subject to no residence restriction imposed by the immigration laws on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is entitled to an exemption under section 8(3) of the Immigration Act 1971 on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is settled in the UK under section 50(2) on *a date*.
*a person* is settled in the UK for section 1(1)(b) through *a parent* on *a date*.

% --- applications, consents and approvals
*a person* made an application on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* makes an application; unknown.
the application of *a person* is in order on *a date*.
the application of *a person* for section 1(4) is in order on *a date*.
the application of *a person* for naturalisation is in order on *a date*.
the application of *a person* made while a minor is in order from *a start* to *an end* on *a date*.
the case of *a person* is approved by the secretary of state on *a date*; undefined.
the secretary of state approves the case of *a person*; unknown.
the approval of the secretary of state for *a person* is given or needed on *a date*.
*a parent* formally consented to the registration of *a person* on *a date*; undefined.
formal consent to the registration of *a person* is given by both parents; unknown.
formal consent to the registration of *a person* is given by one parent; unknown.
formal consent of both parents to the registration of *a person* is given or needed on *a date*.
formal consent of one parent to the registration of *a person* is given or needed on *a date*.
the secretary of state has exercised discretion under section *a section* for *a person*; undefined.
the secretary of state exercises discretion under section *a section* for *a person*; unknown.
discretion of the secretary of state under section *a section* is exercised or needed for *a person*.
*a person* made a declaration of renunciation on *a date*; undefined.
the declaration of renunciation of *a person* is in order on *a date*.
the secretary of state has approved the renunciation of *a person* on *a date*; undefined.
the approval of the renunciation of *a person* is given or needed on *a date*.
*a person* fulfils the requirements of schedule 1 for naturalisation; undefined.

% --- the position before commencement
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies at some time before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies under section 5 of the 1948 act on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies through registration under the 1964 act on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration by virtue of her marriage to *a second person* on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a citizen of the UK and colonies solely by descent on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies through renunciation on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies through renunciation before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* had the right of abode in the UK under the Immigration Act 1971 on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* had the right of abode in the UK under section 2(1)(b) of the Immigration Act 1971 on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* had the right of abode in the UK under section 2(1)(c) of the Immigration Act 1971 on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was registered as a citizen of the UK and colonies in *a place* before *a date*; undefined.
*a place* is mentioned in section 1(3) of the 1948 act; undefined.
*a person* was naturalised in the UK before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was granted a certificate of naturalisation by the secretary of state; undefined.
*a person* was granted a certificate of naturalisation in the islands by the lieutenant governor; undefined.
*a person* became a british subject by residence with a parent under the Naturalisation Act 1870; undefined.
*a person* is naturalised in the UK before commencement.
*a person* would have been entitled to register as a citizen of the UK and colonies by virtue of her marriage to *a second person* on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was a british citizen at some time before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* renounced british citizenship before *a date*; undefined.
*a person* ceased to be a british citizen through renunciation on *a date*.
*a person* ceased to be a british citizen by renunciation since commencement; undefined.
*a person* did not have any citizenship or nationality other than british citizenship on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* did not acquire any citizenship or nationality from *a date* to *a second date*; undefined.
*a person* remained a british citizen from *a date* to *a second date*; undefined.
*a person* is naturalised as a british citizen under section *a section* on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is registered as a british citizen under section *a section* on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is registered under section 8 by virtue of her marriage to *a second person*; undefined.
*a person* is a british dependent territories citizen on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is a british overseas citizen on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is a british subject on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is a british protected person on *a date*; undefined.
section 4 applies to *a person* on *a date*.

% --- commencement
*a person* became a british citizen at commencement.
*a person* became a british citizen by descent at commencement.
*a person* became a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement.
*a person* would have become a british citizen by acquisition at commencement on *a date*.
*a person* would have become a british citizen by descent under section 14(1)(b) on *a date*.
*a person* would have become a british citizen at commencement had he lived.
*a person* would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement had he lived.
*a person* would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement had he lived.
*a person* became or would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement.
*a person* would have become a british citizen at commencement but for renunciation.
*a person* would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement but for renunciation.
*a person* is a british citizen at the birth of *a child* under section 48.
*a person* is a british citizen otherwise than by descent at the birth of *a child* under section 48.
*a person* is a british citizen by descent at the birth of *a child* under section 48.
*a person* is disqualified under section *a section*.
*a person* has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on *a date*.

% --- birth, finding and service
*a person* is found as an abandoned infant on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is found in the UK; undefined.
the claim of *a person* under section 1(2) is invalidated.
it can be shown that *a person* was born outside the UK; undefined.
it can be shown that *a person* was born before commencement; undefined.
the birthday of *a person* is known; undefined.
*a person* was born aboard *a ship or aircraft* registered in the UK; undefined.
*a person* was born aboard *a ship or aircraft* of the UK government; undefined.
*a person* was working outside the UK on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* was employed by *an employer* on *a date*; undefined.
*a person* would have been working outside the UK on *a date* had he lived; undefined.
*a person* would have been employed by *an employer* on *a date* had he lived; undefined.
*a person* was recruited in the UK by *an employer*; undefined.
*a person* was recruited in the UK; undefined.
*a person* was working in crown service under the UK government on *a date*; undefined.
*an employer* is suitable for section 2(1)(b).
*an employer* is crown service under the UK government; undefined.
*an employer* is designated as suitable by the secretary of state under section 2(3); undefined.
the designation of *an employer* is annulled by a House of Parliament; undefined.
*a person* served in crown service under the government of a dependent territory on or before *a date*; undefined.

% --- places
*a place* counts as a foreign country.
*a place* is in the commonwealth.
*a place* counts as a dependent territory; undefined.
*a place* is part of *a second place*.

the knowledge base the British Nationality Act 1981 includes:

% ======================================================================
% The questions the original system offered (its askabout facts)
% ======================================================================

% offset 259895
rule question_citizen with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is a british citizen on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and the person is a british citizen by a way under section a section on the date.

% offset 257448
rule question_descent with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person is a british citizen by descent on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and the person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the date.

% offset 257319
rule question_annulment with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12(3)":
a person is a british citizen by annulment of renunciation on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and the person regains british citizenship by annulment of renunciation under section "12(3)" on the date.

% offset 257541
rule question_naturalise with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 6":
a person is entitled to naturalise as a british citizen on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and the person is entitled to naturalise as a british citizen under section a section on the date.

% offsets 278686, 329365 (recovered from inside damaged records)
rule question_renounce with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12":
a person is entitled to renounce british citizenship on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and the person is entitled to renounce british citizenship under section "12" on the date.

% reconstructed: only a misspelt fact with no arguments survives (offset 257695);
% written by analogy with the five questions above
rule question_register with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and the person is entitled to register as a british citizen as a category under section a section on the date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 1: acquisition by birth or adoption
% ======================================================================

% offset 333174
rule s1_1_a with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(1)(a)":
a person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(1)(a)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is in the UK
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and the birth date is on or after commencement
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and it is not the case that
        the parent had died by commencement
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the parent
    and the parent is a british citizen on the first date.

% offset 289064 (version with a posthumous parent's citizenship at birth, section 48)
rule s1_1_a_48 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(1)(a)":
a person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(1)(a)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is in the UK
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and the birth date is on or after commencement
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent is a british citizen at the birth of the person under section 48.

% offset 334755
rule s1_1_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(1)(b)":
a person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(1)(b)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is in the UK
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and the birth date is on or after commencement
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the parent
    and the person is settled in the UK for section 1(1)(b) through the parent on the first date.

% offset 50739
rule s1_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(2)":
a person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(2)" on a date
    if the person is found as an abandoned infant on a first date
    and the person is found in the UK
    and the first date is on or after commencement
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and it is not the case that
        the claim of the person under section 1(2) is invalidated.

% offsets 166090 - 166600
rule s1_2_invalid_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(2)":
the claim of a person under section 1(2) is invalidated
    if it can be shown that the person was born outside the UK.

rule s1_2_invalid_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(2)":
the claim of a person under section 1(2) is invalidated
    if the birthday of the person is known
    and the person is born on a date
    and it is not the case that
        the date is on or after commencement.

rule s1_2_invalid_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(2)":
the claim of a person under section 1(2) is invalidated
    if it can be shown that the person was born before commencement.

% offset 54009
rule s1_5 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(5)":
a person is a british citizen by adoption under section "1(5)" on a date
    if the person becomes a british citizen from a first date by adoption under section "1(5)"
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

% offsets 54431, 313484 (recovered from inside damaged records)
rule s1_5_from with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(5)":
a person becomes a british citizen from a date by adoption under section "1(5)"
    if the person is adopted as a minor by an order of a UK court on the date
    and the date is on or after commencement
    and a first date is the day before the date
    and it is not the case that
        the person is a british citizen by a way under section a section on the first date
    and an adopter is an adopter of the person
    and the adopter is a british citizen on the date.

% offset 136300 and its twins
rule s1_3_register_minor with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(1)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "a minor" under section "3(1)" on a date
    if the person is a minor from a start to an end
    and the application of the person made while a minor is in order from the start to the end on the date
    and the approval of the secretary of state for the person is given or needed on the date.

% offset 42061
rule s1_4_register with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(4)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "born in the UK" under section "1(4)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is in the UK
    and the person is born after commencement
    and it is not the case that
        the person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(1)(a)" on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(1)(b)" on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the person is a british citizen by birth under section "1(2)" on the date
    and the person is an age years old on the date
    and the age is greater than or equal to 10
    and the person satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4)
    and the application of the person for section 1(4) is in order on the date.

% offset 262823
rule s1_4_residence with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(4)":
a person satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4)
    if the person is born on a birth date
    and a tenth birthday is 10 years after the birth date
    and the person satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4) from the birth date to the tenth birthday.

% offsets 57001, 265025: every year of the first ten, at most 90 days of absence
rule s1_4_residence_end with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(4)":
a person satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4) from a start to an end
    if the start is after or equal to the end.

rule s1_4_residence_year with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(4)":
a person satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4) from a start to an end
    if the start is before the end
    and a next date is 1 years after the start
    and the person was absent from the UK for a number days from the start to the next date
    and the number is less than or equal to 90
    and the person satisfies the residence requirement of section 1(4) from the next date to the end.

% offset 348112
rule s1_4_application with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 1(4)":
the application of a person for section 1(4) is in order on a date
    if the person made an application on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and the person is an age years old on the first date
    and the age is greater than 10.

% ======================================================================
% Section 2: acquisition by descent
% ======================================================================

% offset 346941
rule s2_1_a with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 2(1)(a)":
a person is a british citizen by descent under section "2(1)(a)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the birth date is on or after commencement
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and it is not the case that
        the parent had died by commencement
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the parent
    and the parent is a british citizen on the first date
    and it is not the case that
        the parent is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the first date.

% offset 343026 (a parent in suitable service abroad)
rule s2_1_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 2(1)(b)":
a person is a british citizen by descent under section "2(1)(b)" on a date
    if the person is born outside the UK after commencement
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and it is not the case that
        the parent had died by commencement
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the parent
    and the parent is a british citizen on the first date
    and the parent was working outside the UK on the first date
    and the parent was employed by an employer on the first date
    and the employer is suitable for section 2(1)(b)
    and the parent was recruited in the UK by the employer.

% offset 337600 (a parent who had died by commencement)
rule s2_1_b_dead with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 2(1)(b)":
a person is a british citizen by descent under section "2(1)(b)" on a date
    if the person is born outside the UK after commencement
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent had died by commencement
    and the parent would have become a british citizen at commencement had he lived
    and the parent would have been working outside the UK on the birth date had he lived
    and the parent would have been employed by an employer on the birth date had he lived
    and the employer is suitable for section 2(1)(b)
    and the parent was recruited in the UK by the employer.

% offsets 239284, 314263
rule s2_2_suitable_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 2(2)":
an employer is suitable for section 2(1)(b)
    if the employer is crown service under the UK government.

rule s2_2_suitable_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 2(3)":
an employer is suitable for section 2(1)(b)
    if the employer is designated as suitable by the secretary of state under section 2(3)
    and it is not the case that
        the designation of the employer is annulled by a House of Parliament.

% ======================================================================
% Section 3: registration of minors
% ======================================================================

% offset 21240 (2 copies)
rule s3_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(2)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "a minor" under section "3(2)" on a date
    if the person is born outside the UK after commencement
    and the person made an application on an application date
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the application date is within 1 years after the birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the application date
    and the person is born stateless
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent is a british citizen by descent at the birth of the person under section 48
    and the parent satisfies section "3(3)(b)" on the date.

% offset 1220
rule s3_5 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "a minor" under section "3(5)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person made an application on an application date
    and the person is a minor from a start to an end
    and the application date is in the period from the start to the end
    and the date is after or equal to the application date
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the parent is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the birth date
    and the person is an age years old on the application date
    and the age is greater than or equal to 3
    and the application date is 3 years after a second date
    and the person was in the UK on the second date
    and the person was absent from the UK for a number days from the second date to the application date
    and the number is less than or equal to 270
    and the person satisfies section "3(5)(b) and (c)" on the date for an application made on the application date.

% offset 208882 (both parents alive)
rule s3_5_bc_both with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)(b) and (c)":
a person satisfies section "3(5)(b) and (c)" on a date for an application made on an application date
    if both parents of the person are alive on the application date
    and the application date is 3 years after a first date
    and a mother is the mother of the person
    and the mother was in the UK on the first date
    and the mother was absent from the UK for a first number days from the first date to the application date
    and the first number is less than or equal to 270
    and a father is the father of the person
    and the father was in the UK on the first date
    and the father was absent from the UK for a second number days from the first date to the application date
    and the second number is less than or equal to 270
    and formal consent of both parents to the registration of the person is given or needed on the date.

% offset 208882 (the mother dead)
rule s3_5_bc_one with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)(b) and (c)":
a person satisfies section "3(5)(b) and (c)" on a date for an application made on an application date
    if it is not the case that
        both parents of the person are alive on the application date
    and the mother of the person was dead on the application date
    and a father is the father of the person
    and the application date is 3 years after a first date
    and the father was in the UK on the first date
    and the father was absent from the UK for a number days from the first date to the application date
    and the number is less than or equal to 270
    and formal consent of one parent to the registration of the person is given or needed on the date.

% offset 4289
rule s3_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(3)":
a person satisfies section "3(3)" on a date
    if a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent satisfies section "3(3)(a)" on the date
    and the parent satisfies section "3(3)(b)" on the date
    and the parent satisfies section "3(3)(c)" on the date.

% offset 5357
rule s3_3_b_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(3)(b)":
a person satisfies section "3(3)(b)" on a date
    if a parent is a parent of the person
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and the parent is a british citizen on the birth date
    and it is not the case that
        the parent is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the birth date.

rule s3_3_b_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(3)(b)":
a person satisfies section "3(3)(b)" on a date
    if a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent had died by commencement
    and the parent would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement had he lived.

rule s3_3_b_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(3)(b)":
a person satisfies section "3(3)(b)" on a date
    if a parent is a parent of the person
    and it is not the case that
        the parent had died by commencement
    and the parent became a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement.

% offset 5583
rule s3_3_c with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(3)(c)":
a person satisfies section "3(3)(c)" on a date
    if the date is 3 years after a first date
    and the person satisfies the residence requirement of section 3(3)(c) from the first date to the date.

rule s3_3_c_residence with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(3)(c)":
a person satisfies the residence requirement of section 3(3)(c) from a start to an end
    if the person was in the UK on the start
    and the person was absent from the UK for a number days from the start to the end
    and the number is less than or equal to 270.

% ======================================================================
% Section 4: british dependent territories citizens and others
% ======================================================================

% offset 21240
rule s4_5 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4(5) and 4(6)(a)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "a british dependent territories citizen or similar" under section "4(5)" on a date
    if section 4 applies to the person on the date
    and the person served in crown service under the government of a dependent territory on or before the date
    and the application of the person is in order on the date
    and the approval of the secretary of state for the person is given or needed on the date.

rule s4_applies_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4":
section 4 applies to a person on a date
    if the person is a british dependent territories citizen on the date.

rule s4_applies_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4":
section 4 applies to a person on a date
    if the person is a british overseas citizen on the date.

rule s4_applies_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4":
section 4 applies to a person on a date
    if the person is a british protected person on the date.

rule s4_applies_4 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4":
section 4 applies to a person on a date
    if the person is a british subject on the date.

% offsets 27244 - 28900: the residence conditions of section 4(2); the rule of
% section 4(2) that uses them is lost
rule s4_2_a with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4(2)(a)":
a person satisfies section "4(2)(a)" on a date
    if the date is 5 years after a first date
    and the person was in the UK on the first date
    and the person was absent from the UK for a number days from the first date to the date
    and the number is less than or equal to 450.

rule s4_2_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4(2)(b)":
a person satisfies section "4(2)(b)" on a date
    if the date is 1 years after a first date
    and the person was absent from the UK for a number days from the first date to the date
    and the number is less than or equal to 90.

rule s4_2_b_waived with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4(4)(a)":
a person satisfies section "4(2)(b)" on a date
    if discretion of the secretary of state under section "4(4)(a)" is exercised or needed for the person.

rule s4_2_c with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4(2)(c)":
a person satisfies section "4(2)(c)" on a date
    if the person is subject to no residence restriction imposed by the immigration laws on the date
    and discretion of the secretary of state under section "4(4)(b)" is exercised or needed for the person.

rule s4_2_d with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 4(2)(d)":
a person satisfies section "4(2)(d)" on a date
    if the date is 5 years after a first date
    and it is not the case that
        the person was in the UK in breach of the immigration laws from the first date to the date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 6: naturalisation
% ======================================================================

% offset 74039
rule s6_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 6(1)":
a person is entitled to naturalise as a british citizen under section "6(1)" on a date
    if the person is of full age on the date
    and the person is of full capacity
    and the person fulfils the requirements of schedule 1 for naturalisation
    and the application of the person for naturalisation is in order on the date
    and the approval of the secretary of state for the person is given or needed on the date.

% offset 31786
rule s6_application with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 6":
the application of a person for naturalisation is in order on a date
    if the person made an application on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

% offset 50629
rule naturalised with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 6":
a person is a british citizen by naturalisation under section a section on a date
    if the person is naturalised as a british citizen under section the section on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 8: women by virtue of marriage
% ======================================================================

% offset 161937
rule s8_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 8(3)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "a woman by virtue of marriage" under section "8(3)" on a date
    if the person is female
    and the person made an application on an application date
    and the application date is within 5 years of commencement
    and the person is the wife of a husband on the application date
    and a first date is the eve of commencement
    and the person would have been entitled to register as a citizen of the UK and colonies by virtue of her marriage to the husband on the first date
    and the husband satisfies section "8(3)(b)" on the date
    and the approval of the secretary of state for the person is given or needed on the date.

% offsets 40429, 160300
rule s8_3_b_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 8(3)(b)":
a person satisfies section "8(3)(b)" on a date
    if the person became a british citizen at commencement
    and the person ceased to be a british citizen by renunciation since commencement.

% ======================================================================
% Section 9: by virtue of the father's citizenship; the rule itself is lost
% ======================================================================

% offset 170573
rule s9_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 9(2)":
a person satisfies section "9(2)" on a date
    if a first date is the eve of commencement
    and a father is the father of the person
    and a second date is the earlier of the first date and the death of the father
    and the father was a citizen of the UK and colonies under section 5 of the 1948 act on the second date
    and a mother is the mother of the person
    and the mother is the wife of the father on the second date
    and the father satisfies section "9(2)(b)" on the date.

% offset 170801
rule s9_2_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 9(2)(b)":
a person satisfies section "9(2)(b)" on a date
    if it is not the case that
        the person had died by commencement
    and the person became a british citizen at commencement
    and a first date is the earlier of the date and the death of the person
    and the person remained a british citizen from commencement to the first date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 10: registration following renunciation of citizenship of the UK and colonies
% ======================================================================

% offset 35663
rule s10_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(2)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "following renunciation of citizenship of the UK and colonies" under section "10(2)" on a date
    if the person is of full capacity
    and a first date is the commencement date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies at some time before the first date
    and the person ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies through renunciation before the first date
    and the person satisfies section "10(2)(a) or (b)" on the date
    and the application of the person is in order on the date
    and the approval of the secretary of state for the person is given or needed on the date.

rule s10_2_or_a with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(2)":
a person satisfies section "10(2)(a) or (b)" on a date
    if the person satisfies section "10(2)(a)" on the date.

rule s10_2_or_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(2)":
a person satisfies section "10(2)(a) or (b)" on a date
    if the person satisfies section "10(2)(b)" on the date.

rule s10_2_a with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(2)(a)":
a person satisfies section "10(2)(a)" on a date
    if the person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on the date.

rule s10_2_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(2)(b)":
a person satisfies section "10(2)(b)" on a date
    if the person is female
    and the person had married by the date
    and the person was married to a husband on or before the date
    and the husband has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on the date.

% offsets 84784 - 86200 and twins: section 10(4)
rule s10_4_born_self with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is in the UK.

rule s10_4_born_father with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if a father is the father of the person
    and the birthplace of the father is in the UK.

rule s10_4_born_grandfather with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if a grandfather is the paternal grandfather of the person
    and the birthplace of the grandfather is in the UK.

rule s10_4_naturalised_self with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if the person is naturalised in the UK before commencement
    and the person was naturalised in the UK before the date.

rule s10_4_naturalised_father with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if a father is the father of the person
    and the father is naturalised in the UK before commencement
    and the father was naturalised in the UK before the date.

rule s10_4_naturalised_grandfather with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if a grandfather is the paternal grandfather of the person
    and the grandfather is naturalised in the UK before commencement
    and the grandfather was naturalised in the UK before the date.

rule s10_4_registered_self with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if the person was registered as a citizen of the UK and colonies in a place before the date
    and the place is part of the UK.

rule s10_4_registered_father with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if a father is the father of the person
    and the father was registered as a citizen of the UK and colonies in a place before the date
    and the place is part of the UK.

rule s10_4_registered_grandfather with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 10(4)":
a person has an appropriate qualifying connection with the UK on a date
    if a grandfather is the paternal grandfather of the person
    and the grandfather was registered as a citizen of the UK and colonies in a place before the date
    and the place is mentioned in section 1(3) of the 1948 act.

% ======================================================================
% Section 11: citizens of the UK and colonies at commencement
% ======================================================================

% offset 301243 (not registered)
rule s11_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(1)":
a person is a british citizen by "acquisition at commencement" under section "11(1)" on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and a first date is the eve of commencement
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the first date
    and it is not the case that
        the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration on the first date
    and the person had the right of abode in the UK under the Immigration Act 1971 on the first date.

% offset 129831 (registered: section 11(2) applies)
rule s11_1_registered with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(1)":
a person is a british citizen by "acquisition at commencement" under section "11(1)" on a date
    if the date is on or after commencement
    and a first date is the eve of commencement
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the first date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration on the first date
    and the person satisfies section "11(2)" on the first date
    and the person had the right of abode in the UK under the Immigration Act 1971 on the first date.

% offsets 129831 - 130700
rule s11_2_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(2)":
a person satisfies section "11(2)" on a date
    if it is not the case that
        the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies through registration under the 1964 act on the date.

rule s11_2_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(2)":
a person satisfies section "11(2)" on a date
    if the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies through registration under the 1964 act on the date
    and the person had the right of abode in the UK under section 2(1)(c) of the Immigration Act 1971 on the date.

rule s11_2_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(2)":
a person satisfies section "11(2)" on a date
    if the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies through registration under the 1964 act on the date
    and a mother is the mother of the person
    and the mother had died by commencement
    and the mother would have become a british citizen at commencement had he lived.

% offset 21576 and twins
rule s11_would with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(1)":
a person would have become a british citizen by acquisition at commencement on a date
    if the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration on the date
    and the person satisfies section "11(2)" on the date
    and the person had the right of abode in the UK under the Immigration Act 1971 on the date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 12: renunciation, and its annulment
% ======================================================================

% reconstructed from the damaged copies at offsets 156189, 319002 and 321217:
% each keeps a different part of the rule
rule s12_ceases with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12":
a person ceases to be a british citizen through renunciation under section "12" on a date
    if the person made a declaration of renunciation on a first date
    and the person is of full age for section 12(5) on the date
    and the person is of full capacity
    and the declaration of renunciation of the person is in order on the date
    and the approval of the renunciation of the person is given or needed on the date.

% reconstructed from the damaged copy at offset 321610; the end of the rule is lost
rule s12_entitled with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12(1)":
a person is entitled to renounce british citizenship under section "12" on a date
    if the person is a british citizen on the date
    and the person is of full age for section 12(5) on the date
    and the person is of full capacity.

% offsets 157077 - 157200
rule s12_5_married with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12(5)":
a person is of full age for section 12(5) on a date
    if the person was married on the date.

rule s12_5_not_minor with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12(5)":
a person is of full age for section 12(5) on a date
    if it is not the case that
        the person is a minor on the date.

rule s12_5_is_married with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12(5)":
a person is of full age for section 12(5) on a date
    if the person is married on the date.

% offset 156489
rule s12_declaration with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12":
the declaration of renunciation of a person is in order on a date
    if the person made a declaration of renunciation on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

% offset 158939
rule s12_approval with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12":
the approval of the renunciation of a person is given or needed on a date
    if the person made a declaration of renunciation on a first date
    and the secretary of state has approved the renunciation of the person on a second date
    and the date is after or equal to the second date.

% offset 158404
rule s12_3_annulment with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12(3)":
a person regains british citizenship by annulment of renunciation under section "12(3)" on a date
    if the person was a british citizen at some time before the date
    and the person ceased to be a british citizen through renunciation on a first date
    and the person did not have any citizenship or nationality other than british citizenship on the first date
    and a second date is six months on from the first date
    and the person did not acquire any citizenship or nationality from the first date to the second date
    and the date is after or equal to the second date.

a second date is six months on from a first date
    if the second date is 6 months after the first date.

rule s12_ceased with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 12":
a person ceased to be a british citizen through renunciation on a date
    if the person made a declaration of renunciation on the date
    and the person ceases to be a british citizen through renunciation under section "12" on the date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 13: resumption of citizenship
% ======================================================================

% offset 136143
rule s13_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 13(3)":
a person is entitled to register as a british citizen as "resumption after renunciation" under section "13(3)" on a date
    if the person is of full capacity
    and the person was a british citizen at some time before the date
    and the person renounced british citizenship before the date
    and the application of the person is in order on the date
    and the approval of the secretary of state for the person is given or needed on the date.

% ======================================================================
% Section 14: british citizens by descent
% ======================================================================

rule s14_1_a_descent with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(a)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(a)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born after commencement
    and the person is a british citizen by descent under section "2(1)(a)" on the date.

rule s14_1_a_registered with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(a)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(a)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born after commencement
    and the person is registered as a british citizen under section "3(2)" on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule s14_1_a_registered_9 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(a)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(a)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born after commencement
    and the person is registered as a british citizen under section "9" on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule s14_1_b with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(b)" on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born before commencement
    and it is not the case that
        the person is disqualified under section "14(2)"
    and the person became a british citizen at commencement
    and a first date is the eve of commencement
    and the person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i) to (iv)" on the first date.

rule s14_1_c with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(c)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(c)" on a date
    if the person is born after commencement
    and the person is registered as a british citizen under section "3(1)" on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent is a british citizen at the birth of the person under section 48.

rule s14_1_d with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(d)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(d)" on a date
    if the person is registered as a british citizen under section "5" on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule s14_1_e with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(e)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(e)" on a date
    if the person is female
    and the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born before commencement
    and it is not the case that
        the person is disqualified under section "14(2)"
    and the person is registered as a british citizen under section a section on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and the person is registered under section 8 by virtue of her marriage to a husband
    and the husband ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies through renunciation before commencement
    and the husband would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement but for renunciation.

rule s14_1_f with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(f)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(f)" on a date
    if the person is registered as a british citizen under section "10(2)" on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and a second date is the commencement date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies at some time before the second date
    and the person ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies before the second date
    and the person would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement but for renunciation.

rule s14_1_g with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(g)":
a person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section "14(1)(g)" on a date
    if the person is registered as a british citizen under section "13" on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and the person ceased to be a british citizen through renunciation on a second date
    and a third date is the day before the second date
    and the person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the third date.

rule s14_1_b_any_i with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i) to (iv)" on a date
    if the person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i)" on the date.

rule s14_1_b_any_ii with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i) to (iv)" on a date
    if the person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(ii)" on the date.

rule s14_1_b_any_iii with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i) to (iv)" on a date
    if the person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(iii)" on the date.

rule s14_1_b_any_iv with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i) to (iv)" on a date
    if the person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(iv)" on the date.

% offsets 73260 (recovered from inside a damaged record) and 297715 - 313824
rule s14_1_b_i with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)(i)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i)" on a date
    if the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies under section 5 of the 1948 act on the date.

rule s14_1_b_ii with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)(ii)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(ii)" on a date
    if the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies solely by descent on the date.

rule s14_1_b_iii with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)(iii)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(iii)" on a date
    if the person had the right of abode in the UK under section 2(1)(b) of the Immigration Act 1971 on the date.

rule s14_1_b_iv with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)(iv)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(iv)" on a date
    if the person is female
    and the person had married by the date
    and the person was married to a husband on or before the date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration by virtue of her marriage to the husband on the date
    and the husband became a british citizen by descent at commencement.

rule s14_1_b_iv_dead with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)(iv)":
a person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(iv)" on a date
    if the person is female
    and the person had married by the date
    and the person was married to a husband on or before the date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies by registration by virtue of her marriage to the husband on the date
    and the husband had died by commencement
    and the husband would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement had he lived.

% offsets 52401 - 53300
rule s14_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(2)":
a person is disqualified under section "14(2)"
    if the person is disqualified under section "14(2)(a)".

rule s14_2_a with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(2)(a)":
a person is disqualified under section "14(2)(a)"
    if a father is the father of the person
    and the person is born on a birth date
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the father
    and the father was working outside the UK on the first date
    and the father was working in crown service under the UK government on the first date
    and the father was recruited in the UK.

% offset 22720 and twins: would-have-become rules used by section 14
rule s14_would with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(b)":
a person would have become a british citizen by descent under section 14(1)(b) on a date
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and it is not the case that
        the person is disqualified under section "14(2)"
    and the person satisfies section "14(1)(b)(i) to (iv)" on the date.

% ======================================================================
% Commencement: who became, or would have become, a british citizen
% ======================================================================

% offset 190188: the original asked whether this was known; a scenario may state it
rule commencement_became with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11":
a person became a british citizen at commencement
    if a date is the commencement date
    and the person is a british citizen by a way under section a section on the date.

rule commencement_by_descent with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person became a british citizen by descent at commencement
    if the person became a british citizen at commencement
    and a date is the commencement date
    and the person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the date.

rule commencement_otherwise with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person became a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement
    if the person became a british citizen at commencement
    and a date is the commencement date
    and it is not the case that
        the person is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the date.

rule commencement_if_alive with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 11(1)":
a person would have become a british citizen at commencement had he lived
    if the person died on a date
    and the person was a citizen of the UK and colonies on the date
    and the person would have become a british citizen by acquisition at commencement on the date.

rule commencement_if_alive_descent with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement had he lived
    if the person died on a date
    and the person would have become a british citizen at commencement had he lived
    and the person would have become a british citizen by descent under section 14(1)(b) on the date.

rule commencement_if_alive_otherwise with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement had he lived
    if the person died on a date
    and the person would have become a british citizen at commencement had he lived
    and it is not the case that
        the person would have become a british citizen by descent under section 14(1)(b) on the date.

rule commencement_or_if_alive_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person became or would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement
    if the person became a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement.

rule commencement_or_if_alive_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14":
a person became or would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement
    if the person had died by commencement
    and the person would have become a british citizen otherwise than by descent at commencement had he lived.

rule commencement_renounced with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(f)":
a person would have become a british citizen at commencement but for renunciation
    if the person ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies through renunciation on a date
    and a first date is the day before the date
    and the person would have become a british citizen by acquisition at commencement on the first date.

rule commencement_renounced_descent with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 14(1)(f)":
a person would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement but for renunciation
    if the person would have become a british citizen at commencement but for renunciation
    and the person ceased to be a citizen of the UK and colonies through renunciation on a date
    and a first date is the day before the date
    and the person would have become a british citizen by descent under section 14(1)(b) on the first date.

% offset 141911 and twins: section 48, a parent's citizenship at a child's birth
rule s48 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 48":
a parent is a british citizen at the birth of a child under section 48
    if the child is born on a birth date
    and it is not the case that
        the parent had died by commencement
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the parent
    and the parent is a british citizen on the first date.

rule s48_otherwise with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 48":
a parent is a british citizen otherwise than by descent at the birth of a child under section 48
    if the parent is a british citizen at the birth of the child under section 48
    and the child is born on a birth date
    and a first date is the earlier of the birth date and the death of the parent
    and it is not the case that
        the parent is a british citizen by descent for the purposes of section a section on the first date.

rule s48_descent with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 48":
a parent is a british citizen by descent at the birth of a child under section 48
    if the parent had died by commencement
    and the parent would have become a british citizen by descent at commencement had he lived.

% ======================================================================
% Part 5: interpretation
% ======================================================================

% offset 219849: section 50(7), birth on a ship or aircraft
rule s50_7_registered with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(7)":
the birthplace of a person is in the UK
    if the person was born aboard a ship registered in the UK
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent is a british citizen at the birth of the person under section 48.

rule s50_7_government with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(7)":
the birthplace of a person is in the UK
    if the person was born aboard a ship of the UK government
    and a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent is a british citizen at the birth of the person under section 48.

rule born_in_uk with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the birthplace of a person is in the UK
    if the person is born in a place
    and the place is part of the UK.

rule born_outside_uk with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the birthplace of a person is outside the UK
    if the person is born in a place
    and it is not the case that
        the birthplace of the person is in the UK.

% offset 182227 (recovered from inside a damaged record)
rule born_outside_after with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is born outside the UK after commencement
    if the birthplace of the person is outside the UK
    and the person is born on a date
    and the date is on or after commencement.

rule born_after with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is born after commencement
    if the person is born on a date
    and the date is on or after commencement.

rule born_before with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is born before commencement
    if the person is born on a date
    and the date is prior to commencement.

% offset 1197 (the end of the rule is lost; the three conditions that survive)
rule s50_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(2) and (3)(a)", reconstructed:
a person is settled in the UK under section 50(2) on a date
    if the person is ordinarily resident in the UK on the date
    and the person is subject to no restriction on the period for which he may remain in the UK on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the person is entitled to an exemption under section 8(3) of the Immigration Act 1971 on the date.

% offset 334600
rule s50_4 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(4)":
a person is settled in the UK for section 1(1)(b) through a parent on a date
    if the parent is settled in the UK under section 50(2) on the date.

% offsets 284590, 338001 and 339276: section 50(6)(a)
rule s50_6_a_1 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(6)(a)":
a person is naturalised in the UK before commencement
    if the person was granted a certificate of naturalisation by the secretary of state.

rule s50_6_a_2 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(6)(a)":
a person is naturalised in the UK before commencement
    if the person was granted a certificate of naturalisation in the islands by the lieutenant governor.

rule s50_6_a_3 with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(6)(a)":
a person is naturalised in the UK before commencement
    if the person became a british subject by residence with a parent under the Naturalisation Act 1870.

% offset 83647: section 50(1), what "the UK" means
Great Britain is part of the UK.
Northern Ireland is part of the UK.
the Channel Islands is part of the UK.
the Isle of Man is part of the UK.
the UK is part of the UK.

% offset 93979
rule foreign_country with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(1)":
a place counts as a foreign country
    if it is not the case that
        the place is part of the UK
    and it is not the case that
        the place is equal to the Republic of Ireland
    and it is not the case that
        the place counts as a dependent territory
    and it is not the case that
        the place is in the commonwealth.


