% ======================================================================
% Persons, families and ages
% ======================================================================

rule parent_mother with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(9)":
a person is a parent of a second person
    if the person is the mother of the second person.

rule parent_father with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(9)":
a person is a parent of a second person
    if the person is the father of the second person.

rule grandfather with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is the paternal grandfather of a second person
    if a father is the father of the second person
    and the person is the father of the father.

rule wife with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is the wife of a second person on a date
    if the person was married on the date
    and the second person is the husband of the person on the date.

rule died_before_commencement with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person had died by commencement
    if the person is dead
    and a date is the commencement date
    and the person died before the date.

rule age with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is a number A years old on a date
    if the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is after or equal to the birth date
    and the date is a number M months after the birth date
    and A = M // 12.

rule minor_period with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(11)":
a person is a minor from a date to a second date
    if the person is born on the date
    and the second date is 18 years after the date.

rule minor_on with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(11)":
a person is a minor on a date
    if the person is a minor from a start to an end
    and the date is in the period from the start to the end.

rule minor_at_commencement with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a person is a minor at commencement
    if a date is the commencement date
    and the person is a minor on the date.

rule full_age_date with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(11)":
a person attains full age on a date
    if the person is born on a birth date
    and the date is 18 years after the birth date.

rule full_age with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(11)":
a person is of full age on a date
    if the person is an age years old on the date
    and the age is greater than or equal to 18.

rule full_capacity with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 50(11)":
a person is of full capacity
    if it is not the case that
        the person is of unsound mind.

% ======================================================================
% Applications, consents and approvals: "given or needed"
% ======================================================================

rule application_made with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the application of a person is in order on a date
    if the person made an application on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule application_needed with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the application of a person is in order on a date
    if it is not the case that
        the person made an application on a first date
    and the person makes an application.

rule application_minor_made with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the application of a person made while a minor is in order from a start to an end on a date
    if the person made an application on a first date
    and the first date is in the period from the start to the end
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule application_minor_needed with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the application of a person made while a minor is in order from a start to an end on a date
    if it is not the case that
        the person made an application on a first date
    and the date is in the period from the start to the end
    and the person makes an application.

rule approval_given with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the approval of the secretary of state for a person is given or needed on a date
    if the case of the person is approved by the secretary of state on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule approval_needed with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
the approval of the secretary of state for a person is given or needed on a date
    if it is not the case that
        the case of the person is approved by the secretary of state on a first date
    and the secretary of state approves the case of the person.

% offset 223380 (recovered from inside a damaged record) and 223739
rule consent_both_given with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)(c)":
formal consent of both parents to the registration of a person is given or needed on a date
    if a mother is the mother of the person
    and the mother formally consented to the registration of the person on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date
    and a father is the father of the person
    and the father formally consented to the registration of the person on a second date
    and the date is after or equal to the second date.

rule consent_both_needed with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)(c)":
formal consent of both parents to the registration of a person is given or needed on a date
    if formal consent to the registration of the person is given by both parents.

rule consent_either_given with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)(c)":
formal consent of one parent to the registration of a person is given or needed on a date
    if a parent is a parent of the person
    and the parent formally consented to the registration of the person on a first date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule consent_either_needed with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981 at "section 3(5)(c)":
formal consent of one parent to the registration of a person is given or needed on a date
    if formal consent to the registration of the person is given by one parent.

rule discretion_exercised with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
discretion of the secretary of state under section a section is exercised or needed for a person
    if the secretary of state has exercised discretion under section the section for the person.

rule discretion_needed with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
discretion of the secretary of state under section a section is exercised or needed for a person
    if it is not the case that
        the secretary of state has exercised discretion under section the section for the person
    and the secretary of state exercises discretion under section the section for the person.

% ======================================================================
% Dates
% ======================================================================

% offset 30838: this is how the program recorded commencement (the date of Royal Assent)
1981-10-30 is the commencement date.

rule after_commencement with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is on or after commencement
    if a first date is the commencement date
    and the date is after or equal to the first date.

rule before_commencement with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is prior to commencement
    if a first date is the commencement date
    and the date is before the first date.

rule day_before with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is the day before a second date
    if the second date is 1 days after the date.

rule day_before_commencement with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is the eve of commencement
    if a first date is the commencement date
    and the date is the day before the first date.

rule during with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is in the period from a start to an end
    if the date is after or equal to the start
    and the date is before the end.

rule years_after with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a second date is a number N years after a first date
    if M = 12 * N
    and the second date is M months after the first date.

rule within_years with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is within a number years after a second date
    if a third date is the number years after the second date
    and the date is after or equal to the second date
    and the third date is after or equal to the date.

rule within_years_commencement with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is within a number years of commencement
    if a second date is the commencement date
    and the date is within the number years after the second date.

rule earliest_dead with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is the earlier of a second date and the death of a person
    if the person is dead
    and the person died on a third date
    and the date is the earlier date of the second date and the third date.

rule earliest_alive with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is the earlier of the date and the death of a person
    if it is not the case that
        the person is dead.

rule earliest_first with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is the earlier date of a second date and the date
    if the second date is after or equal to the date.

rule earliest_second with provenance the British Nationality Act 1981:
a date is the earlier date of the date and a second date
    if the second date is after the date.

query british_citizen is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is a british citizen on the date.

query british_citizen_by_descent is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is a british citizen by descent on the date.

query british_citizen_by_annulment_of_renunciation is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is a british citizen by annulment of renunciation on the date.

query entitled_to_register is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is entitled to register as a british citizen on the date.

query entitled_to_naturalise is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is entitled to naturalise as a british citizen on the date.

query entitled_to_renounce is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is entitled to renounce british citizenship on the date.

query how is:
    the question is asked on a date
    and which person is a british citizen by which way under section which section on the date.

% ======================================================================
% Test cases. Each was also run on bna.pl (the SWI-Prolog conversion) with the
% same facts; every person bna.pl names, this program names too (bnaRecovery.md, section 10).
% entitled_to_renounce has no answers in bna.pl, which lost that question.
% ======================================================================

scenario birth_in_uk is:
    the question is asked on 1990-01-01.
    peter is born in London.
    London is part of the UK.
    peter is born on 1985-01-01.
    john is the father of peter.
    john is born on 1950-06-05.
    john was a citizen of the UK and colonies on 1981-10-29.
    john had the right of abode in the UK under the Immigration Act 1971 on 1981-10-29.
    british_citizen expects answers ["the question is asked on 1990-01-01 and peter is a british citizen on 1990-01-01", "the question is asked on 1990-01-01 and john is a british citizen on 1990-01-01"].
    british_citizen_by_descent expects answers [].
    british_citizen_by_annulment_of_renunciation expects answers [].
    entitled_to_register expects answers ["the question is asked on 1990-01-01 and peter is entitled to register as a british citizen on 1990-01-01"] and any unknowns.
    entitled_to_naturalise expects answers [].
    entitled_to_renounce expects answers ["the question is asked on 1990-01-01 and john is entitled to renounce british citizenship on 1990-01-01"].

scenario foundling is:
    the question is asked on 1990-01-01.
    anna is found as an abandoned infant on 1984-05-01.
    anna is found in the UK.
    british_citizen expects answers ["the question is asked on 1990-01-01 and anna is a british citizen on 1990-01-01"].
    british_citizen_by_descent expects answers [].
    british_citizen_by_annulment_of_renunciation expects answers [].
    entitled_to_register expects answers [].
    entitled_to_naturalise expects answers [].
    entitled_to_renounce expects answers ["the question is asked on 1990-01-01 and anna is entitled to renounce british citizenship on 1990-01-01"].

